# The Pi build this executor depends on.
#
# temporalio/pi branch moe/pin-head, a merge of the open fork pull requests: #12 (moe/write-guard,
# a sibling of the stack) and #4 (moe/turn-steps, the top of the stack). Neither head alone has
# everything below. Once they merge, the pin moves to fork main.
#
#   #9 (merged) splits one turn of the agent loop into a model call, its tool calls and a seal.
#   #12 adds SessionManager.setWriteGuard, which is the only place a driver can be sure it still
#      owns the file: the write a model call ends with lands minutes after anything else could
#      have checked.
#   #2 adds prepareStep and recordPrompt on AgentSession: settle what a stopped turn left behind,
#      and record a prompt without a model call, so a worker can drive a session one step at a
#      time.
#   #4 adds modelCall, runToolCall and sealStep, which split a step so each tool call is its own
#      unit of work, and hands the same three to an executor as turn.steps through
#      pi.registerTurnExecutor. A seal records that a turn's turn_end ran, so one retried in
#      another process does not run it again. The seal reads no retry budget off the transcript:
#      the driver carries the count each seal returns into the next one.
# None of it is in the published @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent, so the dependency is a build of
# the fork.
#
# Bump PI_FORK_REF when the PR moves, then re-run scripts/setup-fork.sh.

PI_FORK_REPO=https://github.com/temporalio/pi.git
PI_FORK_REF=5461517979366af8896c55b502e8c6d0d0ca4e11
